# Git Sync Follow-up

When the user asks to sync, merge, or switch branches and local commits are created or a local branch becomes ahead of its tracked remote:

- Push the relevant branch to its remote after verifying the local operation succeeded.
- Do not leave a branch ahead of its remote unless the user explicitly says not to push.
- Still avoid force-push or other destructive git actions unless explicitly requested.
- Report the final branch, remote tracking status, and whether anything remains uncommitted.
